course: dictionary
lesson: 13139
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Use the clues around the word to find the meaning that fits. «The thief made a forcible entry through the back window.» The window was broken, so forcible means done by force, against someone's will.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «Her forcible argument convinced the whole class.» Nobody was pushed or hurt here. Forcible means strong and convincing, because her reasons were good.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. "The thief made a strong and convincing entry" makes no sense, so the first meaning is right. Try each meaning whenever a word could mean two things.
fact: Forcible means done by using force or violence, against someone's will.
fact: «Forcible» can also mean strong and convincing, as in «a forcible argument».
fact: «Forcible entry» means breaking into a place by force.
fact: «Forcibly removed» means taken away by force, against the person's will.
fact: Nobody may use force on your body. If someone does, tell a trusted adult and report it.
exercise: «The thief made a forcible entry through the back window.» What does forcible mean here? | Done with a smile | Done very quietly and slowly | Done early in the morning | *Done by breaking in using force
exercise: «Her forcible argument convinced the whole class.» What does forcible mean in this sentence? | Hidden and secret | *Strong and convincing | Loud and rude | Sleepy and tired
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The guard was forcibly removed from the room.» that shows force was used. | *forcibly | room | guard | from
test: Mia says forcible always means nice and gentle. What does forcible really mean? | Very tiny and light | Nice and gentle, like a kind hug | *Done by force, against someone's will | Sleepy in the sun
test: What is a good check when a word could mean two things? | Wait until the teacher gives you the answer | Skip the word and never think about it again | Guess the first meaning you think of | *Put each meaning into the sentence and see which one makes sense
exam: Which sentence uses forcible to mean strong and convincing? | *«Her forcible argument made everyone listen.» | «The guard was forcibly removed.» | «The thief made a forcible entry.» | «The sun was shining over the hill.»
